cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CrackSegmentation"
abstract: >-
  Interactive Python / OpenCV tool for manually segmenting and annotating
  structural cracks and detachments on photos of building facades, producing
  LabelMe-compatible annotations and training-ready binary masks. Developed
  within the ECHO-TWIN project.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22948009
repository-code: "https://github.com/rob-spina/CrackSegmentation"
url: "https://github.com/rob-spina/CrackSegmentation"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - crack segmentation
  - structural health monitoring
  - image annotation
  - computer vision
  - LabelMe
